WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.267
-Sarah Michelle Gellar!

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.868
-You have the best band.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.901
Do you ever, like -- You just have the best band.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.901
Like, I would just -- I would get so distracted.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.968
Like, I want to talk to you, but I also kinda want to listen.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.834
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah. Very, very lucky.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:14.434
It is so great to see you. You look fantastic.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.067
-Yeah. Subtle. Very subtle. -Thank you.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.000
Yeah, yeah, yeah. They're great and everything.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.434
-They are wonderful. -Yeah, they are wonderful.

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:20.968
-I know. It's been a long time. -How have you been?

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.467
How is everything doing? How's Freddie doing?

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.934
-It's good. I mean, you know, luckily you haven't had drinks

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.801
with him recently, so I haven't lost him

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:30.968
to a foreign country for four months at a time.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.834
True story. A long time ago,

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.801
Freddie went out with Jimmy and his parents.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.400
-My mom and dad. -And -- Yes.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.601
And, um, a few drinks were had.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:40.667
And the next thing -- -They loved him so much.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.100
-Oh. Oh, yeah. I think they were --

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.067
I mean, we were planning to go to your house for Christmas.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.467
-Yeah. My dad was calling him "son" at one point.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.834
-Absolutely. [ Laughter ]

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.901
But, yeah, they got my husband to agree to go to London

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:52.567
for, I don't know, like, three months to do a play.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:55.167
He woke up the next morning, and he was like, "What did I say I'd do?"

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.567
I'm like, "Oh, you're doing a show."

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.133
-Yeah. There was some director or someone there.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.734
And they said, "Yeah, I wrote this play. Do you want to do it?"

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.300
And he agreed that night that we were out.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.234
-And apparently that's binding, so be careful what you drink.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.767
You might wind up in a new show.

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:08.200
-But, alright. So wait. How long have you guys been married?

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.067
-We have been married -- uh, married over 20 years.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.567
-Wow. -I had to think about it.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.200
I had to think about that.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.167
-You guys -- That's the best. You've gotta give him my best.

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.033
And how are the kids? How old are the kids?

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.634
-They're good. Well, you should know --

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.634
Because this is very important that I say this.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:23.968
My daughter wanted me to remind you

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.133
that she is your birthday twin. -She is?

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.901
-And she takes -- she takes a lot of pride in it.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:31.033
But what's funny was my son was also almost your birthday twin.

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.367
Because my kids were --

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.868
So, my daughter, for her third birthday,

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.801
we asked what she wanted, and all she wanted was her brother.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:38.000
But he wasn't due for three weeks.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.968
But apparently my daughter gets what she wants,

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:43.300
and thankfully, for the 12 hours --

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.901
They're the day after, so -- But we almost had two of --

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.801
Both my kids would be your birthday twin.

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:49.100
-September 19th. Virgo.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.834
-Yep. So now September 19th and September 20th.

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:52.467
-What is her name again?

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.067
-My name? -No. Your daughter's name.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.300
-Oh, I was like...

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.501
"We've known each other this long..."

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.234
-Who -- Who are you again? -Sar-ah!

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:01.000
-Sarah, yeah, yeah, yeah. -Sar-ah.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.367
-Just wondering -- Yeah. -Charlotte and Rocky.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:06.400
-Yeah. Charlotte, happy birthday. Rocky, happy birthday.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.567
But hi, Charlotte.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.267
-Sarah. -Oh, my God.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.601
-I really thought you were... -What are you talking about?!

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.000
-You meet a -- You meet a lot of people.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.334
I don't know. -I've known you forever!

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.534
Oh, my gosh. You're one of the --

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.434
By the way, you were one of the best hosts

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:18.868
I've ever worked with on "Saturday Night Live."

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.000
-Aww. -I just want to say.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.267
You were phenomenal. -Thank you.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.467
-I loved working with you every single time.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:23.968
-It was such a dream. And I also --

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.934
The day that I knew that, like, I was finally in

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.133
and had respect was, we were doing a skit one time

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:29.734
and we just couldn't stop laughing.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:32.100
And Lorne yelled at me -- just like he yelled at you.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.167
And I was like, "Oh! He thinks I'm one of the cast."

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:36.167
-Yes! -I was like, "Yes, I made it!

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.868
Lorne yelled at me!" -You feel my pain. Exactly.

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.634
-Then afterwards, I was like, "Oh, I just got yelled at."

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.067
But it was, like, one of those moments

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.367
where, like, I felt good about it.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.901
-Yeah, I mean, you have those things,

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.367
but also we were talking backstage.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.501
We were talking about "Buffy."

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.701
And we were saying that I heard that somewhere --

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:52.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.300
I read somewhere that Dolly Parton

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.467
was an uncredited producer. -Yes.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:03:00.667
Little-known fact. The legend Dolly Parton was a producer.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:03.133
And, you know, we never saw her. Like, we'd get Christmas gifts in the beginning

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:05.434
that would have our name, and I would think, "She doesn't know who I am."

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:08.033
And then one day somebody asked her about it,

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.234
and she complimented the show and my performance.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.100
And I was like, "Oh, I can die now.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.667
Dolly Parton knows who I am and thinks I'm good."

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.868
-No, that's so cool. -So, yeah. But I'm still here.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.100
-I didn't know she --

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.868
I didn't know she was, like, a silent producer.

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.868
-Yeah, little-known fact. Her partner was Sandy Gallin.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.367
-Sandy Gallin. -Yeah.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.634
-No way. -And they produced "Buffy."

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.267
-Isn't that wild? -Yep.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.701
-Now, I want to talk about this new series, "Wolf Pack."

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.000
You -- You executive produce this one here.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.701
Do you ever have any hesitation going back into another,

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.067
like, supernatural type of thing?

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.501
You're like, "I'm not doing 'Buffy.'

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.167
There's not vampires."

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:39.434
-Well, yeah, but there's so -- such difference.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.567
I mean, vampires, wolves. Like, totally different.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.300
-Yeah, yeah. Completely. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.300
-You know, I think there's always hesitation, right?

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.100
Because you don't -- it's hard to have something

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.501
that people are gonna compare it to.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:51.067
But I also love watching and being part of those shows,

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:52.767
so I think it's different enough.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.400
And, you know, a few years have passed since.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.300
-Oh, yeah. -You know, 20.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.834
We don't have to, like, put a number on it,

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.100
but if we're gonna get specific...

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.801
-You don't have to, yeah. -It's been some time.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.200
-How do we describe "Wolf Pack"?

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.634
-Well, I describe it as basically --

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.167
It takes place in the L.A. fires,

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.167
which is something no one's, like, really dealt with.

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.200
But really at a deeper level, it's about anxiety.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.000
It's about finding your pack, finding your people.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.834
-It's two teenagers that kind of bond and then --

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:19.534
-Yeah, so two teenagers get bit when all of the animals

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:23.000
come out during the fire, and they find two other teenagers.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.200
-Can we say what -- what happened?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.400
We have to say it.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.033
-What? They become werewolves? -Yeah.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.734
-Well, I mean -- "Wolf Pack," right?

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:31.234
-Yeah, but you wanna say that.

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:32.400
They actually -- There's werewolves.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.567
-See, this is why they don't like me

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:34.734
to go out and pitch these shows.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.300
'Cause clearly I'm not good at it.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.200
-No, this is all good. -We need to find somebody else.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.000
-So there's two kids -- The two kids, they find --

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.167
They don't know each other. They get bit by the thing.

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:43.868
And there's werewolves? -And there's werewolves.

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:46.000
-That's all we want to talk about. I love this.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.501
-There's werewolves. -I want "Wolf Pack."

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.400
That's what I'm talking about. I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.601
-Starring Sarah. -Starring Sarah.

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:53.767
-Sarah. -Jimmy.

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:55.100
-Jimmy. Nice to meet you. -Nice to meet you.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.334
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.000
Here's Sarah Michelle Gellar in "Wolf Pack."

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.400
Take a look. -I'm so jealous.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.300
-I need your help, Everett.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.100
I need you to help me figure out

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:06.601
who's responsible for the deaths of several people.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:08.033
That includes some of your friends

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.968
who were on that school bus.

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:12.801
♪♪

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:15.734
You're gonna hear that the police suspect arson.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:18.834
That's only part of the truth.

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:21.934
Because it's not just a suspicion.

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:26.300
I know for certain this fire was caused by arson.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.534
I can tell you I'm certain of one other thing.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:32.300
The arsonist is a teenager.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.267
Might even be someone you go to school with.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.234
In fact, it's quite possible

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:40.501
this teenager was on that bus with you.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.234
-Come on. That's how you do it.

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:45.033
[ Cheers and applause ] Sarah Michelle Gellar!

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:48.334
"Wolf Pack" airs Thursdays on Paramount Plus.

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:51.133
More "Tonight Show" after the break. Stick around, everybody.

